@startuml process-view
' ProjectPulse — Process View (4+1 Model)
' Two key workflows shown as sequence diagrams.

skinparam backgroundColor #1a1f2e
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #8b949e
  ActorBorderColor #388bfd
  LifeLineBorderColor #30363d
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #21262d
  ParticipantBorderColor #388bfd
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #21262d
  ParticipantFontColor #e6edf3
  NoteBackgroundColor #161b22
  NoteBorderColor #388bfd
  NoteFontColor #c9d1d9
}
skinparam ArrowFontColor #8b949e

title ProjectPulse — Process View (Stage 2)

' ════════════════════════════════════════
' SEQUENCE 1 — Application Boot / Hydration
' ════════════════════════════════════════
== Workflow 1: Application Bootstrap & API Hydration ==

actor User as U
participant "Browser" as B
participant "data.js" as D
participant "api.js" as A
participant "logic.js" as L
participant "Express Server\n(/api/data)" as S
database "db.json" as DB

U  -> B  : Open URL (http://localhost:3001)
B  -> D  : Parse & execute
D  -> D  : Initialise appData = deep clone of DB
B  -> A  : Parse & execute (defines initFromAPI)
B  -> L  : Parse & execute (defines _boot)

note over L : if typeof initFromAPI === 'function'

L  -> A  : initFromAPI()
A  -> S  : GET /api/data\n(3 s timeout)
S  -> DB : Read all collections
DB --> S : JSON payload
S  --> A : 200 OK { team, tasks, pipeline, ... }
A  -> L  : _mergeInto(appData, data)

note over A,L : On network error → catch() → _boot() anyway

L  -> L  : _boot() — loadState() from localStorage
L  -> L  : syncUIControls(filterRole, filterStatus, ...)
L  -> B  : renderAll() → DOM update

B  --> U : Dashboard displayed

' ════════════════════════════════════════
' SEQUENCE 2 — Mark Task as Done
' ════════════════════════════════════════
== Workflow 2: Mark Task as Done ==

participant "User\n(Dashboard)" as U2
participant "logic.js\n(markDone)" as L2
participant "api.js\n(patchTask)" as A2
participant "Express\n/api/tasks/:id" as S2
database "In-memory\ntasks[]" as DB2

U2 -> L2 : click "Mark as Done" (taskId=X)
L2 -> L2 : mutate appData.tasks[X]\n(status=done, risk=Low, testPass=100)
L2 -> L2 : unshift activity entry
L2 -> A2 : patchTask(X, {status:'done',...})
A2 -> S2 : PATCH /api/tasks/X\n{status, risk, testPass}

note over A2 : fire-and-forget — UI already updated

S2 -> DB2 : tasks[X] = merged fields
DB2 --> S2 : updated task object
S2 --> A2 : 200 OK + task JSON

L2 -> L2  : renderAll()
L2 --> U2 : Task badge turns green

' ════════════════════════════════════════
' SEQUENCE 3 — Scenario Simulation
' ════════════════════════════════════════
== Workflow 3: Simulate Failure Scenario ==

participant "User" as U3
participant "logic.js\n(applyScenario)" as L3

U3 -> L3 : click "Simulate Failure"
L3 -> L3 : Object.assign(appData.pipeline, SCENARIOS.failure.pipeline)
L3 -> L3 : Override delayed task statuses
L3 -> L3 : Push "Cascading System Failure" risk (if not exists)
L3 -> L3 : Push failure incident entry
L3 -> L3 : Update metrics.ops (uptime, responseTime, errorRate)
L3 -> L3 : renderAll()
L3 --> U3 : Health banner turns RED\nRelease blocked

@enduml
